    <name>
      <text>Ghana B9: Complete a table for a linear relation</text>
    </name>

    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;
Complete the table of values for the linear relation
\[
y = {@m@}x + ({@c@}).
\]
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;table border="1"
       cellpadding="8"
       style="border-collapse:collapse;
              text-align:center;"&gt;

&lt;tr&gt;
  &lt;th&gt;\(x\)&lt;/th&gt;
  &lt;td&gt;\({@x1@}\)&lt;/td&gt;
  &lt;td&gt;\({@x2@}\)&lt;/td&gt;
  &lt;td&gt;\({@x3@}\)&lt;/td&gt;
  &lt;td&gt;\({@x4@}\)&lt;/td&gt;
  &lt;td&gt;\({@x5@}\)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;tr&gt;
  &lt;th&gt;\(y\)&lt;/th&gt;

  &lt;td&gt;
    [[input:ans1]]
    [[validation:ans1]]
    [[feedback:prt1]]
  &lt;/td&gt;

  &lt;td&gt;
    [[input:ans2]]
    [[validation:ans2]]
    [[feedback:prt2]]
  &lt;/td&gt;

  &lt;td&gt;
    [[input:ans3]]
    [[validation:ans3]]
    [[feedback:prt3]]
  &lt;/td&gt;

  &lt;td&gt;
    [[input:ans4]]
    [[validation:ans4]]
    [[feedback:prt4]]
  &lt;/td&gt;

  &lt;td&gt;
    [[input:ans5]]
    [[validation:ans5]]
    [[feedback:prt5]]
  &lt;/td&gt;

&lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
Substitute each \(x\)-value into the equation
before entering the corresponding \(y\)-value.
&lt;/p&gt;
      </text>
    </questiontext>


    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text>&lt;h3&gt;Worked solution&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
The relation is
\[
y = {@m@}x + ({@c@}).
\]
For each column, substitute the given value of \(x\).
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
For \(x={@x1@}\):
\[
y=({@m@})({@x1@})+({@c@})
={@y1@}.
\]
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
For \(x={@x2@}\):
\[
y=({@m@})({@x2@})+({@c@})
={@y2@}.
\]
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
For \(x={@x3@}\):
\[
y=({@m@})({@x3@})+({@c@})
={@y3@}.
\]
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
For \(x={@x4@}\):
\[
y=({@m@})({@x4@})+({@c@})
={@y4@}.
\]
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
For \(x={@x5@}\):
\[
y=({@m@})({@x5@})+({@c@})
={@y5@}.
\]
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
Therefore the completed \(y\)-row is
\[
{@y1@},\;
{@y2@},\;
{@y3@},\;
{@y4@},\;
{@y5@}.
\]
&lt;/p&gt;
      </text>
    </generalfeedback>


